# Normalize line endings.
#
# Without this, a Windows editor rewriting a file with CRLF makes git report
# every line as changed. That produced an 18-file, 9,186-line phantom diff with
# zero actual content changes, and would turn any merge into a conflict on
# every line of every file.
#
# text=auto: git normalizes to LF in the repository.
# eol=lf:    checkouts stay LF on every platform, including Windows.
#            Modern Windows tooling handles LF fine, and pinning it means the
#            repo looks identical to everyone regardless of editor.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
